WEBVTT

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.600
Welcome back.

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:04.860
Are you celebrating your team's hard work?

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:08.320
Are you accidentally celebrating a culture of burnout?

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.200
As a leader, you are the primary architect

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.860
of your team's performance culture.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:19.840
A burnout-proof team isn't one that works less.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.160
It's one that works smarter and recovers intentionally.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.220
Your most powerful tool is modeling.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:29.020
Your team won't believe it.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.740
If it's okay to rest, but you say it is,

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:35.040
but then you work all hours.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:38.540
This is the heart of a manager's multiplier effect.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:42.780
You have the ability to make an impact that ripples.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:47.780
A manager notices his team was sending emails at all hours.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:49.860
In their next team meeting, he said,

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.460
I want to be clear,

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:55.100
I do not expect responses outside of work hours.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.240
To protect our team's recovery time,

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:00.860
let's all commit to using the schedule send feature

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:04.420
for any emails written after 6 p.m.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:08.440
You see, he modeled it and the culture shifted.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:12.700
Your play is to model one sustainable performance norm

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:14.180
this week.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:18.600
It could be taking a full lunch break away from your desk,

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.540
ending a meeting five minutes early

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.040
or explicitly signing off at the end of the day.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:31.040
You see, the star player is working constantly.

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:34.060
You see them, you're worried about burnout,

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:37.320
but you also don't want to discourage their commitment.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.460
How do you initiate a conversation

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:41.560
that praises their dedication

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:44.800
while coaching them on sustainable performance?

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.200
Your playbook has a sustainable performance coaching guide

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.320
with conversation starters to help you navigate

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:55.960
this important conversation with both praise and care.

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:58.320
In our final segment for this lesson,

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:02.040
we will cover how to move from modeling good habits

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:06.620
to strategically facilitating recovery for your entire team.
